BTCpu64IosAddAliasMapping de-duped by PeBase equality and returned early,
so a module unloaded and replaced at the same (or an overlapping) PE VA
left FEX translating the NEW module's RIPs into the tombstoned, eventually
zeroed pool copy of the DEAD one. ml356: wevtapi.dll loaded inside a
departed module's registered range; its x64 fast-forward sequence jumped
into the dead copy and executed a page of zeros (udf -> c000001d).

Mirror wine's ios_jit_add_mapping rule: retire every overlapping entry
(Size=0 tombstone + barrier — Module.S's inline walk can never match a
zero-size entry), reuse retired slots, publish Size last.

